# Goal: start N-sample calibration collection (see
# CalibrationBroadcasterConfig::num_samples for the default N — this is
# empty for now since overriding N per-call isn't needed yet, matching the
# project's convention of tuning via YAML params, not per-call args).
---
# Result: final status once collection finishes (success) or is aborted.
# The computed transform itself is not duplicated here — it's already
# broadcast on /tf by calibration_broadcaster_node; read it from there.
bool success
string message
float64 max_spread_deg
float64 mean_spread_deg
# Soft, informational confidence signal — true if the post-outlier-
# rejection max_spread_deg/max position spread are both within
# position_spread_tolerance_cm/orientation_spread_tolerance_deg. Does not
# affect `success` above — a low-confidence result is still a real,
# broadcast, usable calibration; this field exists purely so a caller
# (web UI) can show a warning rather than silently trusting a result that
# may be less accurate than usual, without blocking the workflow on it.
bool is_high_confidence
---
# Feedback: published after each accepted sample.
uint32 samples_collected
uint32 samples_total
# Short, human-readable status text for the current event — e.g. "Sample
# 6 skipped: marker not found (no_yolo_bbox)" or "Waypoint 7: detect call
# timed out after 30.0s". Empty string for the normal "sample recorded
# successfully" feedback (samples_collected/samples_total already convey
# that case fully); this field exists specifically for the
# discard-and-continue/timeout events min_samples_to_finish's soft-fail
# path introduces, giving them a user-visible signal beyond
# calibration_broadcaster_node's own server-side log. Not
# cumulative/history — always just the latest event.
string current_status
# The just-recorded sample's known_chain_frame -> camera candidate pose —
# the same per-sample transform recordSample() computes into
# collected_positions_/collected_orientations_ internally, also surfaced
# here so a caller (web app, RViz via calibration_broadcaster_node's own
# transient per-sample TF broadcast) can visualize how the calibrated
# camera pose estimate is converging sample by sample, not just the final
# averaged result. Zero-valued (default Pose) on any feedback that isn't
# accompanied by a fresh sample.
geometry_msgs/Pose latest_sample_pose